# ── Agent-toolkit material is NEVER committed here ───────────────────────────
# This repository is PUBLIC. Everything `npm run sync-agents` materializes comes
# from the PRIVATE OAKZONE/agent-toolkit repo and is proprietary, so it stays out
# of version control — unlike in the private consumer repos, which do commit it.
#
# Consequence, so the next agent is not surprised: a fresh clone has no rule
# corpus until `npm run sync-agents` is run (it needs access to the private
# toolkit). A cloud agent without that access works from AGENTS.md alone, which
# is why AGENTS.md here is self-contained rather than deferring to the toolkit.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.github/instructions/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.github/workflows/claude.yml
.github/workflows/codex.yml
.vscode/
setup.sh
setup.local.sh

# Working notes from toolkit-alignment and planning runs. They quote the PRIVATE
# toolkit verbatim (rule IDs, template text, sync behaviour), this repository is
# PUBLIC, and `files: ["docs"]` would ship them to every consumer. Same reason as
# the block above: never let toolkit content into a tracked file here.
docs/todo/

